PASS | fort-drum | FAQ JSON-LD == visible | got=[('Why do Fort Drum utilities matter so much?', 'Winter heat. In the North Country, propane, oil or gas heat can push a 3-bedroom’s monthly utilities past $350 in the coldest months. Ask a landlord for last winter’s bills before you sign.'), ('Does 2027 BAH at Fort Drum cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With typical 3-bedroom rent of $1,300–$1,700 and utilities of about $330–$690 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($1,665) lands between −$725 and $35 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2027 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')] | exp=[('Why do Fort Drum utilities matter so much?', 'Winter heat. In the North Country, propane, oil or gas heat can push a 3-bedroom’s monthly utilities past $350 in the coldest months. Ask a landlord for last winter’s bills before you sign.'), ('Does 2027 BAH at Fort Drum cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With typical 3-bedroom rent of $1,300–$1,700 and utilities of about $330–$690 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($1,665) lands between −$725 and $35 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2027 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')]
