PASS | national-capital-region | FAQ JSON-LD == visible | got=[('Do the Pentagon, Fort Belvoir, Fort Myer and Fort McNair all get the same BAH?', 'Yes. ZIPs 22202 (Pentagon), 22060 (Fort Belvoir), 22211 (Fort Myer) and 20319 (Fort McNair) all map to the WASHINGTON, DC METRO AREA (DC053). Fort Meade and Fort Detrick are separate housing areas with different rates.'), ('Does 2027 BAH at National Capital Region cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With typical 3-bedroom rent of $2,800–$3,800 and utilities of about $290–$600 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($3,132) lands between −$1,268 and $42 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2027 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')] | exp=[('Do the Pentagon, Fort Belvoir, Fort Myer and Fort McNair all get the same BAH?', 'Yes. ZIPs 22202 (Pentagon), 22060 (Fort Belvoir), 22211 (Fort Myer) and 20319 (Fort McNair) all map to the WASHINGTON, DC METRO AREA (DC053). Fort Meade and Fort Detrick are separate housing areas with different rates.'), ('Does 2027 BAH at National Capital Region cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With typical 3-bedroom rent of $2,800–$3,800 and utilities of about $290–$600 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($3,132) lands between −$1,268 and $42 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2027 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')]
